+# Aiden offline wake word
+
+The third-party debug companion uses the original INT8 encoder, decoder, joiner, and token list from the [Sherpa-ONNX English GigaSpeech Zipformer keyword-spotting release](https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/download/kws-models/sherpa-onnx-kws-zipformer-gigaspeech-3.3M-2024-01-01.tar.bz2). The model archive identifies Apache 2.0 as its license. The packaged ONNX files have shorter names and their bytes are unchanged.
+
+`keywords.txt` contains the shipped model archive's SentencePiece BPE tokenization of `HEY AIDEN` and `HEY AIDAN`. Both map to the same wake command. The model accepts 16 kHz mono audio on the phone.
+
+The companion uses [Sherpa-ONNX 2.0.1](https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/tag/v2.0.1) (Apache 2.0) and its embedded [ONNX Runtime 1.28.2](https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/tree/v1.28.2) (MIT). The preparation script builds the Android library from the pinned upstream AAR and keeps the original Java classes and ARM64 JNI and ONNX Runtime binaries. The licenses appear in the app’s license view, with additional ONNX Runtime notices beside this file. Wake detection targets ARM64 Android phones.
+
+## SHA-256
+
+| Artifact | SHA-256 |
+| --- | --- |
+| Upstream `sherpa-onnx-2.0.1.aar` | `a8d09d1d32f3eb8520482c6d3d43fae674681c5b050385967c70a3c2c9bf0ee7` |
+| Upstream GigaSpeech model archive | `f170013b4716e41b62b9bfd809687c207cef798ef9bc6534d524e17af9b6561a` |
+| `encoder.int8.onnx` | `1e721676515bcd42a186979733981213c66c80db680e1cc582dfedf3be76e678` |
+| `decoder.int8.onnx` | `e40ff43297abe815e8898494c17e71bba2152d9d40fa3eb803f75d0f7533329a` |
+| `joiner.int8.onnx` | `eae9da0c7e1e6c6a3f4cc42d167899c388f6c6701b94cb96320e4f55df79624c` |
+| `tokens.txt` | `fd2ded4050a55d2b1578870ba8697d02371980217806b7558bd0a5cc60f3ba53` |
+| `keywords.txt` | `84bfff6f956df0a6fba0c1ee72425a339daa3ce5dc5d84252633bc10390d7fce` |
+
+The threshold of 0.12 with four active paths detected 18 of 24 synthetic wake phrases on the Mac and falsely activated on one of 72 distractors, `Hey Hayden`, across eight macOS voices. The phone's microphone, recognition reliability, background behavior, and power use require a device test.
